han crocodile  himself in fact the list of similarities  between the two warlords is  so long that i will move through it  fairly quickly here  not to make this video unnecessarily  long  let's start with the more obvious  parallels and then move a bit deeper  on the most basic level both the second  saga of pre-time skip  alabaster and the second saga of  post-time skip dresrosa  are about a kingdom that is suffering  under the rule of one of the shichibukai  one controlled by a crocodile and the  other by a flamingo  going with the animal theme of the  warlords also  if you're like me and for some reason  have completely missed this super  obvious theme until now  here's a quick overview crocodile is a  crocodile  doflamingo is a flamingo mihawk is a  hawk  kuma literally means bear in japanese  hancock is of course a boa constrictor  jimbei means whale shark in japanese  and finally gekkomoria has actually two  animals  there's obviously the gecko but putting  his name together  gekkomoria komori actually means bat in  japanese  there if you weren't aware of that fact  yet now you know  getting back to topic the flamingo and  crocodile share  a lot more than just a superficial theme  both were the leaders of powerful  criminal organizations  with a number of devil fruit users  including a bomber  someone who can change their weight  someone who can turn their body into  weapons  a power related to art and someone who  can move freely underground  both the baroque works as well as the  donkey hut family have themed code names  one with numbers the other with playing  cards  as a result both mr zero and joker  operated under the facade of celebrated  heroes in their respective countries  committing dark dealings that  contributed to the country's  deterioration  both were trading illegal substances as  part of this scheme  dance powder and sad and both of them  have mastered the devil fruit powers to  high levels able to severely distort the  surrounding environments  both of them at first seemed to get  decapitated  crocodile by vivi and dophi by curos  however both of them easily avoid any  harm by displaying their full skills  oh yeah and for some weird reason both  of them also seem to have a thing for  draped furry coats  but this is far from all let's move to a  more personal level now  even from a plot and character  perspective the flamingo  is clearly referencing crocodile  storyline  first of all both were present at  roger's funeral  being inspired to advance their efforts  to reach the top of the pirate world  both aim to do so by first establishing  control over an entire country  however both of them also earned the  scorn of the country's princess  both vivi and viola went undercover in  their respective organizations  to oppose their evil schemes and protect  their fathers  king cobra and king riku both flamingo  and crocodiles see their subordinates as  tools to advance their own goals  this can be seen especially well in how  they treat those who do not perform well  enough  crocodile completely disregarded galdino  and doflamingo lost any interest  whatsoever in bellamy  after his failure against luffy  exploiting his admiration for him  and i think we can take this all the way  to their respective conflicts with luffy  because in both cases it needed luffy to  uncover their true face  and liberate the country from the  tyranny at first  both crocodile and dophi seem superior  to luffy  and in both cases luffy manages to take  them out in the end  anyway also as a quick side note the way  that luffy destroys doflamingo's string  clone  is very similar to crocodile's defeat as  they both are sent  up to the ceiling and were beaten up by  an attack which involves luffy punching  them multiple times  until the ceiling gets destroyed as they  fall to the ground  and ultimately both of them not only  lost their status as warlords  but also ended up in level 6 of impul  down  as you can see the parallels between  both villains are  endless and i think it should be  self-evident that doflamingo  is strongly inspired by crocodile's role  pre-time skill  so now you might say well if doflamingo  is just a copy of crocodile  doesn't that really make crocodile the  better villain so  let's talk about why i think that  doflamingo is superior here from a  storytelling perspective  the most fundamental assumption here is  that good writers  improve over the course of their career  they learn  what works what doesn't how to structure  things better  and how to improve their characters and  while for most authors this will happen  over the course of multiple books  screenplays and stories oda has been  writing the same storyline for over  20 years and so all of his trial and  error  as well as all of his experience and  improvement are visible throughout the  same story  and so as a direct result of this i  think that oda made it a point  to revisit alabasta that was already  great  and wanted to prove that he can make it  even a little bit better  a similar setting but better  a similar story but better  now this doesn't mean in any way that i  dislike alabaster even in the slightest  just the opposite the fact that  alabaster was  such a fantastic saga was the thing that  made dressrosa  what it is in the first place also as  one big caveat here i'm strictly talking  about the manga  the anime adaptation of dressrosa was in  my personal opinion  way worse than the manga while the anime  did really well with alabaster  now that being said drastirosa is woven  way better into the overall flow of the  story and the overarching events  than alabaster did once that story was  over  it basically felt a little bit like a  hard cut  similarly dresrosa integrates many of  the major themes of the story  just a little bit better than alabasta  does  for example the helplessness of the  marines in dressrosa  has way more weight and fujitora's  experience with luffy  happens on a more fundamental level i  think than with smoker  whose transition happens over a longer  period of time  even an admiral could do nothing in the  face of the warlord system  but in the end fujitora actually  abolished it  but moving on to the villains themselves  i think it's great that oda made  doflamingo  what crocodile actually aspired to be  crocodile wanted to gain control over  the country  and build his power from there  doflamingo actually  managed to do so he completely overthrew  the king  and drooled openly  as a result i think that in the final  moments of both  battles the position of luffy and the  villain  are extremely important to the symbolism  of the arc  and theme against crocodile luffy is  below him and defeats him by  punching him up into the sky revealing  him as the crook and monster that he was  to all of alabasta  by literally throwing him into the light  luffy being below him during the final  moments represents luffy's climb and  eventual triumph over crocodile  as the underdog recovering from his  previous losses  it's a true struggle for luffy to punch  crocodile into the open and through  bedrock  further symbolizing the barrier  crocodile has created to protect himself  from the public  now luffy versus doflamingo on the other  hand completely  contrasts this luffy is now above the  villain  symbolically representing that luffy is  now the one with the upper hand  doflamingo has already been revealed to  the country of dressrosa  as the monster he is and so they're  fighting in the sky  and being watched by everyone on the  island  luffy's final attack against dophie is a  complete stomp  with not much that can be done to stop  it the  ground underneath them being demolished  is symbolic of the foundation of lies  that the country was built upon being  crushed  this change of position is further  symbolized in the techniques that luffy  uses to defeat them  luffy defeat a crocodile single attack  with a storm of punches  while doflamingo's many-phased attack  was broken through with  one huge punch  i think it's clear that these two scenes  are meant to mirror each other  and so once again oda uses all the good  he did with crocodile  to enhance doflamingo and so i think  that both crocodile  and doflamingo are fantastic characters  however i think that dophi is superior  in the sense that oda was able to build  on  improve and expand what he did with  crocodile  in addition to all of that i also think  that doflamingo's character overall  is one of the most complex in the story  so far  so if you want to learn more about that  i recommend that you check out my  character analysis on him here  thanks guys peace

